        "Genetec AutoVu is municipal / parking ALPR — reads plates at lots and roadside. Name-only when advertised. Pattern match, not that camera. Look with your eyes." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_138)
        "Iteris roadside Bluetooth travel-time reader (Vantage Velocity, now BlueTOAD Spectra / Spectra CV). Samples phones, headsets, and in-car Bluetooth as vehicles pass; matching the same ID at two points gives speed. About 100 m. A sample, not a full count. Quiet or Ethernet-only cabinets may not advertise. Spectra CV also uses 5.9 GHz C-V2X, which Fieldwatch cannot hear. IEEE Iteris OUI can also hit other Iteris roadside kit. Pattern match, not that cabinet." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_139)
        "BLIP Systems BlipTrack roadside Bluetooth/Wi-Fi travel-time sensor. Same job as BlueTOAD Spectra: samples passing phones and in-car radios at two points for speed. Quiet or Ethernet-only cabinets may not advertise. Pattern match, not that cabinet." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_140)
        "Hanwha Vision / Wisenet camera (ex-Samsung Techwin). Common on commercial CCTV and some public poles." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_141)
        "Hanwha Vision / Wisenet cameras. Common on commercial CCTV and some public poles. A *_WISENET setup SSID is the stronger hit; IEEE 00:09:18 is Samsung Techwin. Pattern match, not that camera. Look with your eyes." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_142)
        "Uniview / UNV / Uniarch camera. Common on commercial CCTV and some public poles." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_143)
        "Uniview / UNV cameras. Common on commercial CCTV and some public poles. IEEE Zhejiang Uniview OUIs or a Uniview / UNV- name. Pattern match, not that camera. Look with your eyes." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_144)
        "Rhombus cloud camera. BLE is loudest when the camera is unregistered or offline." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_145)
        "Rhombus cloud cameras on buildings and some public sites. IEEE CC:47:BD or a Rhombus name. BLE often only while unregistered or offline. Pattern match, not that camera. Look with your eyes." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_146)
        "Rekor highway or transit plate reader." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_147)
        "Rekor is highway / transit ALPR — reads plates on roads and at checkpoints. Name-only. Pattern match, not that camera. Look with your eyes." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_148)
        "Axon body-worn camera, in-car system, dock, or TASER. Quiet or LTE-only units will not appear." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_149)
        "Axon body-worn, in-car (Fleet), dock, or TASER gear. IEEE OUI 00:25:DF is Axon Enterprise. Body 3/4 often advertise BLE on that public OUI while worn. A name like Axon Body is a pattern, not that officer. Quiet or LTE-only units will not appear. The word Axon also hits some ZTE phones. Look with your eyes. Not identity." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_150)
        "WatchGuard Video body-worn or in-car camera (now Motorola). Not the WatchGuard firewall company. Patrol units may stay quiet." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_151)
        "WatchGuard Video body-worn or in-car (VISTA / V300 family). IEEE OUI 00:1D:96 is WatchGuard Video, not the WatchGuard firewall company. Patrol units may stay quiet. Pattern match, not identity. Look with your eyes." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_152)
        "Digital Ally body-worn or in-car camera (FirstVu / EVO). Quiet or LTE-only units will not appear." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_153)
        "Digital Ally body-worn or in-car (FirstVu / EVO family). IEEE OUI 00:23:BD is Digital Ally, Inc. — camera gear, not a chip vendor. Patrol units may stay on LTE and stay quiet. Pattern match, not that officer. Look with your eyes. Not identity." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_154)
        "Reveal Media / BodyWorn camera. Common in UK and some US agencies. Quiet units will not appear." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_155)
        "Reveal Media body-worn camera (D-series / BodyWorn). Name-only when advertised. Patrol units may stay quiet. Pattern match, not that officer. Look with your eyes." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_156)
        "Wolfcom body-worn or in-car camera. Quiet units will not appear." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_157)
        "Wolfcom body-worn or in-car camera. Name-only when advertised. Patrol units may stay quiet. Pattern match, not that officer. Look with your eyes." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_158)
