        "Tattile ALPR camera, common on European roads and some US sites." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_169)
        "Tattile plate readers on roads and at gates. Name-only when advertised. Pattern match, not that camera. Look with your eyes." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_170)
        "LiveView Technologies (LVT) solar surveillance trailer. Most units are cellular-only and will not appear." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_171)
        "LVT / LiveView solar camera trailer — parking lots, construction, some city parks. Video and sometimes plates. Most units use cellular and stay quiet on Wi-Fi/BLE. A LiveView or LVT- name is a pattern, not that trailer. Look with your eyes." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_172)
        "UniFi / Ubiquiti name on Wi-Fi or BLE. Prefer UniFi AP for BSSID hits. Instant cameras stay on UniFi Protect." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_173)
        "UniFi / Ubiquiti Wi-Fi access point (including airMAX / AmpliFi). Renamed SSIDs still hit on the board vendor or Ubiquiti vendor tag. Instant cameras stay on UniFi Protect." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_174)
        "Cheap hobby UART module advertised under a default name (HM-10, JDY, CC41, ESP32 BLE). Common on printers, cars, and DIY. Fieldwatch does not see Classic HC-05/HC-06." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_175)
        "These default BLE serial names are cheap hobby modules. Some pump/ATM overlays have used boards like this so someone nearby can pull data over Bluetooth. The same modules show up on printers, cars, and DIY. If this radio is loud next to a card reader, treat it with caution and look with your eyes. Not proof of a skimmer. A miss is not a clean bill (name changed, Classic HC-05/HC-06, or cellular). Fieldwatch does not connect and does not try default PINs. Fieldwatch does not see Classic HC-05/HC-06." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_176)
        "Ray-Ban Meta / Oakley Meta smart glasses, or a Quest / other Meta wearable." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_177)
        "Meta / Luxottica BLE — often Ray-Ban Meta smart glasses. The same company IDs show up on Quest headsets and other Meta wearables. Not proof someone is recording. A miss is not a clean bill (paired and quiet, asleep, or a different brand). Look with your eyes." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_178)
        "Snap Spectacles or other Snap BLE product." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_179)
