        "Vuzix smart glasses or other Vuzix BLE wearable." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_181)
        "Vuzix BLE glasses. Not proof of recording. A miss is not a clean bill (paired and quiet, asleep, or a different brand). Look with your eyes." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_182)
        "Brilliant Labs Frame AR glasses." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_183)
        "Brilliant Labs Frame AR glasses. BLE service 7A230001. Not proof someone is recording. A miss is not a clean bill (off, or a different brand). Look with your eyes." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_184)
        "Even Realities G1 glasses. Name-only (Even G1). Nordic UART is too common to use as a rule." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_185)
        "Even Realities G1 glasses. Name-only when advertised (Even G1). Not proof of recording. A miss is not a clean bill (off, renamed, or paired and quiet). Look with your eyes." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_186)
        "Hak5 WiFi Pineapple setup or management AP. Cloned café SSIDs from PineAP look like ordinary Wi-Fi and will not hit this row." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_187)
        "Hak5 WiFi Pineapple setup or management AP (Pineapple_XXXX). That is the admin radio, not every rogue SSID PineAP might impersonate — those look like ordinary café Wi-Fi. A miss is not a clean bill (renamed, or only cloning). Pattern match, not identity. Look with your eyes." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_188)
        "Flipper Zero (or other Flipper Devices). Default name starts with Flipper; custom firmware can hide it." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_189)
        "Flipper Zero (or other Flipper Devices) BLE. Default name starts with Flipper; newer units use IEEE OUI 0C:FA:22. Custom firmware can change the name and MAC. Not proof of an attack. A miss is not a clean bill (Bluetooth off, or renamed). Look with your eyes." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_190)
        "Pwnagotchi-style Wi-Fi handshake collector. Classic units use a distinctive BSSID and the name pwnagotchi." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_191)
        "Pwnagotchi-style Wi-Fi handshake collector. Classic units beacon BSSID de:ad:be:ef:de:ad. A pwnagotchi name is a pattern. Not proof of an attack. Look with your eyes." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_192)
        "ESP32 Marauder or Spacehuhn-style Wi-Fi deauther on a default name. Same boards are DIY; renamed units miss." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_193)
        "ESP32 Marauder or Spacehuhn-style Wi-Fi deauther default names. Same boards are DIY. Not proof of an attack. A miss is not a clean bill (renamed). Look with your eyes." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_194)
        "GhostESP ESP32 audit firmware. Default setup AP is GhostNet. Same boards are DIY; renamed units miss." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_195)
        "GhostESP ESP32 audit firmware default AP (GhostNet). Same boards are DIY. Not proof of an attack. A miss is not a clean bill (renamed). Look with your eyes." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_196)
        "Bruce ESP32 pentest firmware. Default setup AP is BruceNet. Same boards are DIY; renamed units and evil-portal SSIDs miss." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_197)
        "Bruce ESP32 pentest firmware default AP (BruceNet). Same boards are DIY. Evil-portal SSIDs look like ordinary Wi-Fi and will not hit this row. Not proof of an attack. Look with your eyes." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_198)
        "Porkchop pentest firmware on a Cardputer or Cheap Yellow Display. Default AP name PORKCHOP. BLE spam that spoofs Apple/Android is not this row." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_199)
        "M5PORKCHOP / Porkchop — pocket Wi-Fi pentest firmware (Cardputer or Cheap Yellow Display). Default CYD remote AP is named PORKCHOP. BACON-mode fake APs brand vendor IE 50:52:4B. A miss is not a clean bill (renamed, passive only, or no AP). Pattern match, not identity, not proof of an attack. Look with your eyes." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_200)
        "Nintendo Pokémon GO Plus or Plus + wrist accessory. Not a Joy-Con or Switch." -> UiText.text(R.string.catalog_201)
